{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3PhFbNbxBeZTP5zZeBk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HHpcLh92UjoB424YcW1hTS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"Pass `{ client: true }` to keep the render function in the client\nbundle after [`microbuild`](#microbuild) strips it:\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"The static `render` needs the server render support module, which\nbuilds the host tag and serializes props. The `microtags/htm`\ntemplater loads it, on the server and in the browser. Code that calls\na component's `render` static directly, without the templater, must\nimport [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support) once.\nWithout it, `render` throws an error naming that module.\n\n```ts\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\nimport { MyCounter } from './components.js'\n\nconst markup = MyCounter.render({ start: 5 })\n```\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> This is a breaking change in 0.0.x. Before it, `render` worked with\n> no extra import.\n\nPass `{ client: true }` to keep the render function in the client\nbundle after [`microbuild`](#microbuild) strips it:\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\nold=\"\"\"---\n\n### `microtags/build`\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"---\n\n### `microtags/render-support`\n\nThe host-tag builder, prop serializers and attribute escaping that a\ncomponent's static `render` uses. Import it for its side effect:\n\n```ts\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\n```\n\nIt is separate from core so that a client bundle with every\n`.render` link stripped leaves this code out. The `microtags/htm`\ntemplater imports it already, so only code that calls a `render`\nstatic without the templater needs this import. See\n[ADR-009](./docs/adr/ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md).\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/build`\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnpm run toc 2>&1 | tail -1; git dif