{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3Pon2cRfVTT68UXTozM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Calling a component's `render` static with no templater and no support import throws an error that names the support module\n[x] After importing the server templater, `render` produces the same host HTML as before, and every existing SSR exact-string assertion passes unchanged\n[x] After the browser templater creates a host, `render` works without a separate support import\n[x] Core's size-limit entry is lowered to the ADR-009 number and `npm run size` passes\n[x] `npm run build`, `npm run test:ssr`, `npm test`, `npm run test:hydration` and `npm run lint` pass\n\nAll five checklist items are done, and the full gate passes.\n\nThe host-tag builder, the prop serializers and attribute escaping now live in a new module, `src/render-support.ts`, which is exported as `microtags/render-support`. It uses the global-symbol registration that ADR-009 chose.\n\nCore keeps the prop metadata, now including the `boolean` and `json` kinds, and installs a small `render` static. That static looks up the support module through the global symbol. If nothing has registered it, it throws `microtags: render needs \"microtags/render-support\"`.\n\nThe server templater imports the support module when it loads. The browser templater registers it each time it creates a host.\n\n**Sizes:**\n\n| Bundle | Before | After | Limit |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Core | under 4.3 kB | 3.93 kB | lowered from 4.3 to 3.95 kB |\n| Server templater | — | 1.93 kB | unchanged (5 kB) |\n| Browser templater | under 4.95 kB | 5.18 kB | raised from 4.95 to 5.2 kB |\n\nThe browser templater goes over its old limit because it now carries the support module. I raised the limit using the spec's rule (measured size rounded up to the next 0.05 kB) and noted it in ADR-007. To get core under 3.95 kB I shortened the error message, which saved about 30 B. It still names the module.\n\n**Tests:**\n- **SSR:** a new test runs a small fixture in its own Node process with no templater and checks that `render` throws and names the module. It runs separately because the SSR suite itself imports the templater. The existing exact-string assertions failed after the core change and passed again once the server templater imported the support module; I didn't edit any of them.\n- **Browser:** a new test clears the registry symbol, mounts a kept host, and then calls `render`. It failed until the browser templater registered the module when creating a host.\n- **Gate:** lint, build, `npm run size`, `test:ssr` (114/114) and `npm test` (415/415) pass, along with `test:hydration`, `test:plugins`, `test:build`, `test:cli` and `test:hydration-dev`. The first `npm test` run hit `EADDRINUSE` on port 8123 (another run held it), so I waited and reran.\n\nAs a quick check, a bundle with every render link stripped has no support module and no escape table. The formal plugins-suite check and the transform's injected import belong to ticket 14.\n\n**Docs:**\n- **README:** a breaking-change note for code that calls `render` directly, and a new `microtags/render-support` section. The TOC rerun also removed some entries that pointed at headings that no longer exist.\n- **ADRs:** a note on ADR-005, a correction and a size note on ADR-007, and the final numbers on ADR-009.\n- **AGENTS.md:** the \"Builder and serialization\" section is rewritten for the split, and new coercer types now point at `src/render-support.ts`.\n\nEverything is in two commits; the notes file is uncommitted, as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1091,"cache_read_input_tokens":108589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1091},"output_tokens":692,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10b72dcd-fe8f-4051-b896-6c085ba039d7","uuid":"c5622656-bfec-4570-be81-014cae1e574e","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:30:19.092Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Pomj1TLph2KLV7jr3u"}
